# React Web (retentio-web-test)

## Stack

- **Build**: Vite 7, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS 3
- **UI**: React 18, React Router 6, lightweight components in `src/components/ui/`
- **API**: `src/lib/api.ts` — `request()` to backend; base URL from `VITE_API_URL` (default `http://localhost:8080`)
- **Auth**: `AuthContext` + JWT in `localStorage` (`wordupx_token`)
- **i18n**: `LocaleContext` + `src/locales/` (en/zh string modules)
- **Tests**: Vitest + Testing Library (`*.test.tsx` colocated or under `src/`)

## File organization

```
src/
├── components/     # Feature + UI components (catalog/, deck/, facts/, ui/)
├── contexts/       # Auth, locale
├── hooks/
├── lib/            # api.ts, tags, import/export helpers
├── locales/        # Static copy modules
├── pages/          # Route-level screens
└── routes.tsx      # React Router config + ProtectedRoute
```

## Patterns

- API calls go through `src/lib/api.ts` — do not scatter raw `fetch` in components.
- Public routes: `/`, `/catalog/:id`, `/login`, `/manual`, `/research`. Protected: `/decks`, `/profile`, etc.
- Match existing component style: functional components, hooks, Tailwind utility classes.
- Prefer extending existing types in `api.ts` over ad-hoc response shapes.

## Checks before commit

```bash
npm test -- --run          # or scoped: npm test -- --run src/lib/api.test.ts
npm run build
```

Dev backend URL: see `docs/development.md` (`VITE_API_URL`, `./utils/run-dev.sh`).
